title: The config file is parsed as one blob - the documented sample config cannot
  work
updated: 2026-10-21T20:14:16Z
---

In _build_mods the config is read with io(config)->slurp. slurp returns the whole file as one string, and the map over it therefore produces one rule instead of one rule per line.

The sample config eg/conf has three lines:

    HomeHive|AqHive
    homehive|aqhive
    hh%ah

Parsed as one blob, the first rule gets the from-part HomeHive and a to-part that contains the line breaks and the other two rules inside it. The tool therefore never behaves as its own documentation describes.

Work:
- split the file into lines before mapping over them (IO::All gives the lines directly, or split the slurped content on newlines)
- one rule per line: the kind, the from-part and the to-part
- a line that is empty or only whitespace is skipped; a line with neither a pipe nor a percent is a rule of an unknown kind and has to be reported instead of silently dropped
- the log line in BUILD prints the from-part and the to-part of every rule; it must not warn on a malformed rule
- add a test that parses a config with more than one rule and pins the number of rules and their content

Obsolete: the card was written against the 2014 code on origin/master. On main (release 1.000, rewrite of 2026-03-06) the config is read with Path::Tiny lines({chomp=>1}), one rule per line, split with limit 2. Nothing to do.
